90","verifiedAt":"2026-08-27","collectedAt":"2026-08-27"},"divisionVintage":"TIGER_GENZ2025"},{"ocdId":"ocd-division/country:us/state:az/school_district:empire_elementary_district","statement":"There is no Empire Elementary School District No. 37 governing board race on the November 3, 2026 ballot. Three positions were up and nobody filed, so the Board of Supervisors cancelled the election on 2026-08-11 and recorded THREE (3) VACANCIES on the district’s governing board.","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Pima County Board of Supervisors, agenda item 25 of 2026-08-11 (File ID 20624, matter 21690), “2026 General Election — School District Cancellations”, requested by the School Superintendent and APPROVED 2026-08-11","sourceUrl":"https://pima.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=21690","verifiedAt":"2026-08-27","collectedAt":"2026-08-27"},"divisionVintage":"TIGER_GENZ2025"},{"ocdId":"ocd-division/country:us/state:az/school_district:sahuarita_unified_district","statement":"Sahuarita Unified School District No. 30 has a governing board race on the November 3, 2026 ballot: two positions, with John Sparks and Raul Rodriguez having filed. It is not among the districts whose election the Board of Supervisors cancelled as uncontested on 2026-08-11.","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Pima County Board of Supervisors, agenda item 25 of 2026-08-11 (File ID 20624, matter 21690), “2026 General Election — School District Cancellations”, requested by the School Superintendent and APPROVED 2026-08-11","sourceUrl":"https://pima.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=21690","verifiedAt":"2026-08-27","collectedAt":"2026-08-27"},"divisionVintage":"TIGER_GENZ2025"}],"contests":[{"id":"ballot-az-pima:governor","type":"CANDIDACY","ocdId":"ocd-division/country:us/state:az","title":"Governor","voteFor":1,"scopeNote":"The general-election nominees and qualified write-in candidates are verified against the Secretary of State canvass and write-in list and the Citizens Clean Elections Commission voter guide