November 3 general-election roster, including qualified write-in candidates.","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Arizona Secretary of State","sourceUrl":"https://apps.azsos.gov/election/2026/canvass/20260806_Primary_Canvass.pdf?download=1","collectedAt":"2026-10-15T04:04:22.911340+00:00","verifiedAt":"2026-10-15T04:04:22.911340+00:00","quote":"(REP) Paul Gosar *"},"filing":{"id":"az-sos-2026:us-house-9","publishedTitle":"U.S. Representative - District No. 9","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Arizona Secretary of State","sourceUrl":"https://azsos.gov/sites/default/files/docs/2026-Candidate-Nominations-and-Petitions-Filed-0330.pdf","collectedAt":"2026-09-01"}},"identity":{"identityId":"az-2026:contest:us-house-9","level":"FEDERAL","financeFilingAuthority":"Federal Election Commission"}}],"election":{"id":"az-2026-11-03","date":"2026-11-03","name":"2026 General Election","state":"AZ"},"measures":[{"id":"ballot-az-pima:prop-425:question","contestId":"ballot-az-pima:prop-425","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Pima County, Permanent Base Adjustment — Ballot Language","sourceUrl":"https://content.civicplus.com/api/assets/az-pimacounty/55aa379c-bc22-47fe-8b7c-d10dab0ade8c/permanent-base-adjustment-proposition-pdf.pdf","verifiedAt":"2026-08-27","collectedAt":"2026-08-27"},"questionText":"Pursuant to the Arizona State Constitution, Pima County seeks voter approval to permanently adjust the expenditure base of the County as determined by the Economic Estimates Commission. The County seeks an adjustment of $70,000,000. A “YES” vote shall have the effect of allowing Pima County to adjust its 1979-80 base expenditure limit. A “NO” vote shall have the effect of not allowing Pima County to adjust its 1979-80 base expenditure limit.","officialStatement":"Official Title: A resolution proposing a permanent adjustment to the state-imposed 1979-80 expenditure base for Pima County. Summary analysis: if approved, the County’s 1979-80 base expenditure limitation will be increased by $70,000,000 adjusted each future year for population and inflation growth since 1979-80. With voter approval, in fiscal year 2027-2028 the County’s expenditure limitation will increase by $610,086,481, from $817,131,286 to $1,427,217,767. Referred to the people by the Pima County Board of Supervisors by resolution 2026-23, passed 2026-04-21."},{"id":"ballot-az-pima:prop-423:question","contestId":"ballot-az-pima:prop-423","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Pima County School Superintendent, 2026 School District Special Elections (proposition number); Vail Unified School District No. 20 Notice of Election (question and fiscal terms)","sourceUrl":"https://www.schools.pima.gov/","verifiedAt":"2026-08-27","collectedAt":"2026-08-27"},"questionText":"BUDGET OVERRIDE CONTINUATION, YES / NO — whether Vail Unified School District No. 20 of Pima County, Arizona may continue to exceed the revenue control limit by not more than 12.5% per fiscal year, for fiscal years 2027/2028 and the next six fiscal years.","officialStatement":"From the district’s statutory Notice of Election: a special election consolidated with the General Election of November 3, 2026, under A.R.S. § 15-481(P). The budget effect is approximately $5,102,762 above the alternate budget for 2027/2028, at an estimated continuation of $1.61 per $100 of secondary assessed valuation. The governing board adopted the calling resolution on 2026-06-02. Arguments were due to the Pima County School Superintendent by 5:00 p.m. on 2026-08-07."},{"id":"ballot-az-pima:prop-428:question","contestId":"ballot-az-pima:prop-428","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Pima County School Superintendent, 2026 School District Special Elections","sourceUrl":"https://www.schools.pima.gov/","verifiedAt":"2026-08-27","collectedAt":"2026-08-27"},"questionText":"A 15% Maintenance and Operations Budget Override Continuation for Sahuarita Unified School District, to be considered by the voters of the district at the election of November 3, 2026.","officialStatement":null},{"id":"ballot-az-pima:prop-429:question","contestId":"ballot-az-pima:prop-429","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Pima County School Superintendent, 2026 School District Special Elections","sourceUrl":"https://www.schools.pima.gov/","verifiedAt":"2026-08-27","collectedAt":"2026-08-27"},"questionText":"A 15% Maintenance and Operations Budget Override Continuation for Tanque Verde Unified School District, to be considered by the voters of the district at the election of November 3, 2026.","officialStatement":null}],"candidacies":[{"id":"ballot-az-pima:governor:hobbs-katie","slogan":null,"contestId":"ballot-az-pima:governor","givenName":"Katie","incumbent":null,"familyName":"Hobbs","partyLabel":"Democratic","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Arizona Secretary of State","sourceUrl":"https://azsos.gov/sites/default/files/docs/2026-Candidate-Nominations-and-Petitions-Filed-0330.pdf","verifiedAt":"2026-08-14","collectedAt":"2026-08-14"},"websiteUrl":null,"identity":{"nameForms":[{"form":"katie hobbs","rules":["AS_PUBLISHED"]}],"committees":[{"basis":"name, exact Arizona seat and election cycle all agree with the certified-ballot row","agency":"Arizona Secretary of State — See The Money","committeeId":"201800057","registeredName":"Elect Katie Hobbs"}],"identityId":"az-2026:governor:hobbs-katie","candidacyAuthority":"Arizona Secretary of State — candidate filings","candidacySourceUrl":"https://azsos.gov/sites/default/files/docs/2026-Candidate-Nominations-and-Petitions-Filed-0330.pdf"},"filing":{"id":"az-sos-2026:governor:hobbs-katie","filingDate":"February 25, 2026","provenance":{"sourceOrg":"Arizona Secretary of State","sourceUrl":"https://azsos.gov/sites/default/files/docs/2026-Candidate-Nominations-and-Petitions-Filed-0330.pdf","collectedAt":"2026-09-01"},"publishedName":"Hobbs, Katie","signaturesFiled":8226,"heldIdentityJoin":{"rule":"AS_PUBLISHED","matchedForm":"katie hobbs","heldCandidacyId":"ballot-az-pima:governor:hobbs-katie","heldPublishedName":"Katie Hobbs"}}},{"id":"ballot-az-pima:governor:hourih